% fancy_dress: a Picat model from DCP Rosetta.
%
% Mr. Greenfan wants to give a dress party where the male guests must wear green dresses. The following rules are
% given: 1. if someone wears a green tie he has to wear a green shirt; 2. a guest who wears green socks or a green
% shirt must also wear a green tie or a green hat; 3. a guest wearing a green shirt or a green hat or who does not
% wear green socks must wear a green tie; 4. a guest who is not dressed according to rules 1-3 must pay a $11
% entrance fee. Mr Greenguest wants to participate but owns only a green shirt (otherwise he would have to pay one
% for $9). He could buy a green tie for $10, a green hat (used) for $2 and green socks for $12. What is the cheapest
% solution for Mr Greenguest to participate?
%
%   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/fancy_dress.html
% Save this model as model.pi and run it (Picat 3.9, https://picat-lang.org) with:
%   picat model.pi
import cp.

model(_Data, Vars, Outputs, Options) =>
    % each choice is 1 when the guest wears that item, 0 otherwise
    T :: 0..1,                             % green tie, bought for $10
    H :: 0..1,                             % green hat, bought for $2
    R :: 0..1,                             % green shirt, already owned: costs nothing
    S :: 0..1,                             % green socks, bought for $12
    F :: 0..1,                             % entrance fee of $11
    % rule 1 holds: a guest who wears a green tie wears a green shirt
    B1 #<=> (T #=< R),
    % rule 2 holds: a guest wearing green socks or a green shirt wears a green tie or a green hat
    B2 #<=> ((S + R #= 0) #\/ (T + H #>= 1)),
    % rule 3 holds: a guest wearing a green shirt or a green hat, or not wearing green socks, wears a green tie
    B3 #<=> (((R + H #= 0) #/\ (S #= 1)) #\/ (T #= 1)),
    % rule 4: the entrance fee is paid when one of rules 1-3 does not hold
    Dressed #<=> (B1 #/\ B2 #/\ B3),
    F #= 1 - Dressed,
    Cost #= 10 * T + 2 * H + 11 * F + 12 * S,
    Vars = [T, H, R, S, F],
    Outputs = [t = T, h = H, r = R, s = S, n = F],
    % the cheapest way to take part
    Options = [$min(Cost)].

main =>
    model(new_map(), Vars, Outputs, Options),
    solve(Options, Vars),
    solve(vars(Outputs)),
    foreach(Name = Value in Outputs)
        printf("%w = %w\n", Name, Value)
    end.
